>>>>DECUS Floppy interchange information

	This floppy contains the OS/8 to WPS floppy converter, WPFLOP,
the OS/8 to RT-11 converter, RTFLOP, and supporting programs. The
information necessary to operate each of these is given in the
appropriate documentation file as follows:

RTFLOP - RTFLOP.DC OS/8 to RT-11 floppy interchange
WPFLOP - WPFLOP.DC (Hard copy file) WPS to OS/8 converter
         WPFLOP.IN (Same info, for scopes, etc.)
ADVENT - ADVENT.DC OS/8 Adventure version 2
VTEDIT - VTEDIT.DC Improved TECO V7 screen editor.

         COSHAN.DC Information on the COS compatible Floppy
                   disk handlers, and RXFIX.

	Included is a copy if Jim van Zee's DIRECT V7 modified for
upper/lower case outputs, and the save image of TECO V7.

	The program REMEM allows the OS/8 CCL remembrances to be printed
on the console. This program is written in MACREL, and uses the file
REMEM.MA.

	The BATCH stream, SCOPE.BI, is used to patch the FORTRAN 4
run-time system (FRTS) to allow scope type terminal rubouts. To reverse
the changes, use NOSCOP.BI.

	The copy of ADVENTURE included is a considerable improvement
over the original submission. It allows upper/lower case text output
and a keyboard typeahead buffer. Also, the program only need be initialized
once, and the game can be suspended and resumed later. Finally, the size
of the secondary text storage file has been reduced to 145 blocks (from
250.) See the file ADVENT.DC for more details.
